# echo_emac_sph_en

Enables Split Header (SPH) on all EMAC instances (emac0, emac1, emac2).

By default SPH is disabled. Applying this overlay adds the `snps,sph`
property, which causes the driver to skip setting STMMAC_FLAG_SPH_DISABLE,
enabling SPH in the DMA engine.

## emac0
- SPH: enabled

## emac1
- SPH: enabled

## emac2
- SPH: enabled
